      "message": "So on macOS I\u0027m building with ASAN, using `SkTypeface_Fontations::MakeFromStream` directly in `ResourceFontCollection` to make the fonts, and removed the `UNIX_ONLY` bits to run these tests. When `SkParagraph_EmojiParagraph` runs ASAN emits `runtime error: load of value 111, which is not a valid value for type \u0027bool\u0027` with various values for the value. Putting a watch on the location doesn\u0027t break, so I\u0027m assuming it isn\u0027t being set. In this case everything looks hermetic, so I\u0027m not sure why this isn\u0027t happening on Linux.",
